-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the C family's arithmetic types
-- C and C++ name scalar types whose kind is the implementation's: a type's kind, size and
-- alignment are functions of the Target, and so are the integer promotions and the usual
-- arithmetic conversions (C17, ISO/IEC 9899:2018, 6.3.1.1 “Boolean, characters, and integers” and 6.3.1.8 “Usual arithmetic conversions”; C++20 [conv.prom], [expr.arith.conv]).
-- (char8_t, char16_t, char32_t, wchar_t and enumerations are their underlying types: the
-- reader names those. long double is not here: see the track's Limits.)
data CTy = ct-bool | ct-char | ct-schar | ct-uchar | ct-short | ct-ushort | ct-int | ct-uint
         | ct-long | ct-ulong | ct-llong | ct-ullong | ct-int128 | ct-uint128
         | ct-float | ct-double | ct-ptr
